---
// The first technical feature, concept: the CDC entry's opening rebuilt for progressive disclosure. A 30-second
// summary, who it is for, one simple overview that reflows on phones, then a reading path into the verified detail.
// All statements are a subset of the published entry and its evidence record.
import ConceptLayout from '../../layouts/ConceptLayout.astro';
import CdcOverview from '../../components/concepts/CdcOverview.astro';
import { url } from '../../utils/url';
const entry = url('/architecture/log-based-cdc-into-a-warehouse/');
---

<ConceptLayout title="Log-based CDC into a warehouse" label="shared page for A, B and C: the entry's new opening" current="architecture">
  <article class="container-wide cdc-c" aria-labelledby="cdc-title">
    <header class="cdc-c__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Reference blueprint · Data engineering</p>
      <h1 id="cdc-title">Log-based change data capture into an analytical warehouse</h1>
    </header>

    <section class="cdc-c__summary" aria-labelledby="summary-title">
      <h2 id="summary-title">In 30 seconds</h2>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>The problem</dt>
          <dd>Keep warehouse tables in step with a live database, without querying it on a timer.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>The shape</dt>
          <dd>Read changes from the database's log, land every change, keep the newest per key, and apply only changes newer than what is stored.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>The one thing to remember</dt>
          <dd>Changes can arrive twice after a restart. The warehouse must make duplicates harmless, and a commit-ordered log position is what makes that possible.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Who it's for</dt>
          <dd>Engineers designing or reviewing a CDC pipeline into Snowflake, BigQuery or a similar warehouse.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="cdc-c__overview" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
      <h2 id="overview-title">The idea in one picture</h2>
      <CdcOverview headingId="cdc-ov" />
      <p class="cdc-c__scope">
        <strong>What this picture leaves out:</strong> which tools carry the changes (a Kafka topic or files in object
        storage), monitoring, reconciliation and recovery. Those come next, one at a time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="cdc-c__path" aria-labelledby="path-title">
      <h2 id="path-title">Read on</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><a href={`${entry}#the-blueprint`}>The full blueprint</a>: every component, with product examples and numbered steps.</li>
        <li><a href={`${entry}#failure-and-recovery`}>What happens on a restart</a>: duplicates, replays, and why the target still converges.</li>
        <li><a href={`${entry}#deduplicate-before-every-merge`}>The merge in SQL</a>: an illustrative sketch with its assumptions, not drop-in production code.</li>
        <li><a href={`${entry}#operating-it`}>Operating it</a>: log retention, lag and reconciliation.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="cdc-c__note">
        On a phone, the full blueprint keeps its detail and scrolls sideways; this overview and the text description give
        the whole idea without scrolling.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</ConceptLayout>

<style>
  .cdc-c {
    padding-block: var(--s-8) var(--s-6);
  }

  .cdc-c__head h1 {
    max-width: 24ch;
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-6);
  }

  .cdc-c h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-4);
  }

  .cdc-c__summary {
    background: var(--c-parchment);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--s-6);
    max-width: 64rem;
  }

  .cdc-c__summary dl {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--s-5) var(--s-7);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .cdc-c__summary dt {
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: var(--s-1);
  }

  .cdc-c__summary dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .cdc-c__overview,
  .cdc-c__path {
    margin-top: var(--s-7);
  }

  .cdc-c__scope,
  .cdc-c__note {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--c-graphite);
  }

  .cdc-c__path ol {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding-left: 1.3em;
  }

  .cdc-c__path li + li {
    margin-top: var(--s-3);
  }

  .cdc-c__path a {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .cdc-c__summary dl {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .cdc-c__summary {
      padding: var(--s-5);
    }
  }
</style>
